I went inside the café.
A smiling woman was standing behind the counter.
Her name is Sunita.
She has been running this café for many years.
I looked at her and smiled.
"Namaste, my name is Maya," I said.
"I have come here as a volunteer."
Sunita-tai warmly welcomed me.
"Namaste Maya, welcome!" she said.
"Is this your first day?" she asked.
"Yes, this is my first day," I answered.
Sunita-tai gave me an apron.
"Put on this apron and get ready," she said, smiling.
I put on the apron and thanked her.
"I will teach you all the work," Sunita-tai said.
"Will you teach me to make coffee?"
I asked.
"Yes, we will start from there," she said.
Sunita-tai is very kind and experienced.
I was ready to learn a lot from her.
